      "assistant": "The upper hub on `actuator.ocad.d` is now 64 mm in diameter (was 52 mm) and 48 mm tall (was 32 mm). The change passed its checks in a dry run before I applied it, and the part rebuilt cleanly.\n\n- **Mass:** 609.23 g → 764.09 g (+154.9 g).\n- **Size:** the overall part is now 178 × 110 × 48 mm, up from 178 × 110 × 32 mm. The hub is the tallest feature, so only the height changed.\n- **Holes:** the shaft bore depth follows the hub height, so the 24 mm bore still goes all the way through. The bearing counterbore at the top is unchanged.\n\n**What the preview shows:** the hub is clearly taller and wider. It sits on the 72 mm lower hub, leaving a 4 mm ledge around it. The 24 mm bore, the 8 bolt holes, the base plate and the two mounting ears are all intact.\n\nThe six radial reinforcement ribs can't be seen in the picture. They extend 36 mm from the centre, which is exactly the lower hub's radius, and they're shorter than it, so they sit inside it. This change didn't touch the ribs, so it was very likely the same before, but you may want to lengthen them if they're meant to show."
